      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242955",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/19/19e9c40d07c899aee8531995cf2299a6904bfc62650d72407784bb6b43da5a02.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the parallel lines $l$ and $n$ are crossed by the transversal $t$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $\u22204$ and $\u22205$ are supplementary\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u22208$ and $\u22205$ are supplementary | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $m\u22208 + m\u22205 = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\u22208\u2245\u22204$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u22208 = m\u22204$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $m\u22204 + m\u22205 = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $\u22204$ and $\u22205$ are supplementary | {{field-6}} |"
