      ":question/problem": "![](images/b7/b7e83ceb8b8c124a0a0b7b53c25996ce49bf156df591e7ed97cd49b5ff66c7e6.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the parallel lines $r$ and $s$ are crossed by the transversal $t$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $m\u22201 + m\u22208 = 180^{\u2218}$.\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u22206\u2245\u22208$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $\u22202\u2245\u22206$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\u22202\u2245\u22208$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u22202 = m\u22208$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $\u22201$ and $\u22202$ are supplementary | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $m\u22201 + m\u22202 = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 7 | $m\u22201 + m\u22208 = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-7}} |"
